# KafDesk — product constraints for agents

## Local Kafka test stack

- OK under `share/` for the developer’s machine (gitignored)
- Do not put Docker/broker howto in the main README
- Do not delete a running local stack the user is testing on unless they ask

## Size reality (do not “optimize” the wrong thing)

- Installed Electron app ≈ **100MB+** is normal (Chromium). Do not chase “400MB → tiny SPA”.
- Dev folder bloat is usually `node_modules/electron` + local `release/*.dmg` (gitignored), not UI features.
- Prefer fewer deps; never add heavy UI kits, chart libs, or full syntax highlighters without need.
- Keep produce/consume paths lean: no unbounded message buffers; cap lists (consume limit, bulk ≤2000, logs buffer).

## Stability / resilience (prefer these when touching Kafka/IPC)

- Surface errors in the main banner / active panel (not only the connections drawer)
- Timeouts on produce / SR encode; never leave UI `busy` forever
- Any path that sets UI offline must `disconnect()` the main-process session (no ghosts)
- Tail runtime errors → IPC `kafka:tailError` + stop consumer
- Clamp consume limit in the service (UI is not enough)
- One Kafka session in `kafkaService`; do not expand `useKafdeskApp.ts` with unrelated UI

## Code hygiene

- Match existing style; no drive-by refactors
- No Kafka howto fluff in main README
- When asked to “optimize”, ask whether they mean **installer size**, **runtime memory**, or **code structure** — then act on that
